# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# A run on a GPU whose positions stop being numbers fails with
# SimulationError instead of ending the process (#168,
# D[gpu-position-guard]), scenario overlap of Inputs/python_position_guard.py:
# two particles that are not bonded, on top of one another, with PME, with
# the matrix (deterministic) and with groups. In double and mixed precision
# the simulation keeps the state it began from, and another simulation runs
# on the device.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_position_guard.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU overlap | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: overlap Double: fails after step 0 and keeps its state; another simulation runs: {{.*}}far outside the cell
# CHECK: overlap Double groups: fails after step 0 and keeps its state
# CHECK: overlap Mixed: fails after step 0 and keeps its state
# CHECK: overlap Mixed groups: fails after step 0 and keeps its state
# CHECK: position guard overlap passed
